  "details": "There's probably some more refined version of this idea that would work better, but I was wondering what would be the harm in essentially being able to drop a static version of a test avatar in a world? Since test avatars are completely local, you'd be the only one who could see it, right? But it'd be useful for testing Physbones and Dynamics in-client on your own.\n\nEdit: Just an additional thought, but obviously it could be useful to also be able to control at least the test dummy's expressions menu while you have it deployed, but I dunno how difficult that would be to actually do in practice.",
